From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:50:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: glymur: Extend usb_0/usb_1 QMPPHY
 description for USB4

The USB4 part of the QMP combo PHY needs one more GCC clock, the P2RR2P
(PHY-to-Router, Router-to-PHY) pipe clock, enabled before the PHY can be
initialised in USB4 mode. The qmp-combo USB4 support looks it up as
"p2rr2p_pipe" and refuses USB4 mode when it is missing. Hamoa got the
same description in the series that added that driver support:

  https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260908-topic-usb4phy-v5-5-73aac69578ef@oss.qualcomm.com

Add it to usb_0_qmpphy and usb_1_qmpphy. The driver enables the clock
only on entry to USB4 mode, so USB3 and DisplayPort operation of these
PHYs does not change. Only usb_0_qmpphy has been run in USB4 mode.
usb_2_qmpphy has the same clock (GCC_USB4_2_PHY_P2RR2P_PIPE_CLK) and is
not changed here.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi
index 209ba917c0b..10d29f92fda 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi
@@ -2531,11 +2531,13 @@ usb_0_qmpphy: phy@fd5000 {
 			clocks = <&gcc GCC_USB3_PRIM_PHY_AUX_CLK>,
 				 <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>,
 				 <&gcc GCC_USB3_PRIM_PHY_COM_AUX_CLK>,
-				 <&gcc GCC_USB3_PRIM_PHY_PIPE_CLK>;
+				 <&gcc GCC_USB3_PRIM_PHY_PIPE_CLK>,
+				 <&gcc GCC_USB4_0_PHY_P2RR2P_PIPE_CLK>;
 			clock-names = "aux",
 				      "ref",
 				      "com_aux",
-				      "usb3_pipe";
+				      "usb3_pipe",
+				      "p2rr2p_pipe";
 
 			resets = <&gcc GCC_USB3_PHY_PRIM_BCR>,
 				 <&gcc GCC_USB3PHY_PHY_PRIM_BCR>;
@@ -2604,11 +2606,13 @@ usb_1_qmpphy: phy@fde000 {
 			clocks = <&gcc GCC_USB3_SEC_PHY_AUX_CLK>,
 				 <&tcsr TCSR_USB4_1_CLKREF_EN>,
 				 <&gcc GCC_USB3_SEC_PHY_COM_AUX_CLK>,
-				 <&gcc GCC_USB3_SEC_PHY_PIPE_CLK>;
+				 <&gcc GCC_USB3_SEC_PHY_PIPE_CLK>,
+				 <&gcc GCC_USB4_1_PHY_P2RR2P_PIPE_CLK>;
 			clock-names = "aux",
 				      "ref",
 				      "com_aux",
-				      "usb3_pipe";
+				      "usb3_pipe",
+				      "p2rr2p_pipe";
 
 			power-domains = <&gcc GCC_USB_1_PHY_GDSC>;
 
-- 
